target
crates/*/target
**/target/
contracts/out
contracts/cache
contracts/broadcast
contracts/lib
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
.e2e-logs
sig-store-data
sig-store-data-p6
sig-store-data-p7
*-state.json
*.json.tmp
validator*.toml
keeper*.toml
# these carry inline private_key values; COPY . . would bake them into the
# builder layer even though the runtime stage only copies the binaries.
docker/configs/*.toml
docs
report.md
.git
# Generated stacks, deploy records and local configs: real RPC keys, validator
# and keeper private keys, Solana keypairs. `COPY . .` in the builder stage
# would bake any of them into an image layer (audit round 4, LOW).
docker/*/configs
docker/*/.env
docker/*/keys
docker/production/*/.env
docker/production/*/configs
docker/production/*/secrets
.solana
scripts/*.config.local
scripts/run.config.local
config/*.local.json
config/deployments
sig-store-data*
# root-level TOMLs are the ad-hoc service configs the test suites write (they
# carry private_key); `*` does not cross `/`, so crate manifests are untouched.
*.toml
!Cargo.toml
frontend/.env.local
.env
# The `# secrets` block at the top of .gitignore. A .dockerignore pattern is
# anchored at the context root (no implicit `**/` like git), so each is written
# for every depth; without these a keystore or wallet anywhere in the tree is
# copied into the builder layer (audit round 5, LOW).
**/.env
**/secrets
**/keystore.json
**/bundlr_wallet.json
# Contract deploy env files carry deployer keys.
contracts/fixtures/swap-deploy.env
contracts/fixtures/xswap-*.env
